@startuml installation-and-first-run
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

' Installation from zero and the first run of the main loop: the root is
' instantiated from a pinned, audited template package (no upstream to us),
' one root package installs everything, commands are built from source,
' the first run takes branch A (local model, after stating the download)
' or branch B (semi-automatic harness setup), then channels, pairing with or
' without a screen, the first process and the login agent.
' Sources: main loop spec DRAFT v0.1 §6, §10.6, §11.3; curator-playbook
' process configuration DRAFT v3.5 §2.3, §8.1, §8.6; curator-inference-manager.

title Installation and first run
caption Sources: main loop DRAFT v0.1 §6, §10.6, §11.3; process configuration v3.5 §2.3, §8.1, §8.6

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor $SERVICE
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $SERVICE_LINE
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $COMMITTED
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $COMMITTED_LINE

start
:Install Curator
(script from the website or Homebrew);
:<i>curator apiary init</i>: instantiate the root from the
pinned, audited template package into <U+007E>/apiary
(the person's own repository, no upstream to us);
:Resolve the one root entry, the keeper package:
board tool, session-host tooling,
designer, librarian, sysadmin, watchdog roles, profiles;
:Build the commands from source
(go-v1 driver, pinned Go toolchain);
:Initialize the main loop's board; first commit;
if (Hardware meets the published minimum?) then (yes)
  :State the download: engine and model size,
  disk space, expected time; ask the person;
  if (Person accepts?) then (yes)
    :Install the engine package and a small local model
    (curator-inference-manager);
    :Start the main loop on the local model;
    :Questionnaire: which subscriptions and harnesses?
    Add runtime bindings;
  else (no, set up a harness instead)
    :Semi-automatic harness setup
    (as in the other branch);
  endif
else (no)
  :Detect installed harnesses and logins,
  print the shortest install and login steps,
  check the result;
  :The first working harness becomes the default,
  start the main loop on it;
endif
:Offer channels: messengers through waggle providers
(terminal until then: <i>keeper attach</i>);
if (Node has a screen or a terminal the person sees?) then (yes)
  :Pair the companion app by QR code;
else (headless)
  :Pair by a short code over SSH and compare the
  authentication string, or relay from a paired workstation;
endif
:Keys exchanged and pinned;
:The person asks; the main loop proposes processes
from published packages; the designer creates one;
:The person confirms (companion app or OS authentication);
:The main loop starts the process's root orchestrator;
:Register the login agent that runs <i>keeper up</i> at every login;
stop

@enduml
